ew weeks we've been  working with three really outstanding  groups  uh council of chief state school  officers  chiefs for change and the council of  great city schools to really build out a  10-point framework on key elements that  need to be addressed in any recovery  effort and then really start to  disseminate that and figure out what are  the best practices best organizations  uh and and tools and resources that can  be implemented in each one of those  areas so concretely we know that much of  the learning loss need for acceleration  has been  created by the digital divide we still  have eight to 12 million students who  don't have regular access either to  equipment or excessive access to the  internet we need to solve that problem  and hopefully  seven billion of the dollars that are  going through that stimulus package are  designed to go through the fcc and start  to address it we're gonna have to  continue to work with districts and  states to both solve the problem in the  short term but then in the long term but  then you know what are the strategies  that are research-based that can be  helpful curriculum is really important  end of your courses is really important  opportunities to go on khan academy and  do the extra homework is really  important but they're also just  individual needs like tutoring we've  been lucky to work with a variety of  different tutoring groups that have seen  real advances of you know acceleration  of one to two years in a year of  tutoring so  it'll really be about identifying those  best practices and coordinating  i'm sure like you i really have the  opportunity to talk to a lot of  superintendents and chiefs around the  country it's one of the  joys of my job and i have to say i've  been blown away by how thoughtful people  are  absorbing this amount of money in ways  that are is sustainable over time and  really enables us to build back better  but build back braver is going to be  crucial and i i think you know in the 